payload.description:
ERROR-class follow-through on asp-26e/asp-5a8/asp-5be/asp-fef (all merged 2026-07-22 as standalone scripts/check_*.py + fixtures). The standalone-script shape satisfies each pebble's fixture-level acceptance but NOT the point of the rule set: enforcement reaches consumers ONLY through the Fixit rule-pack ([tool.fixit] enable = ["aspergillus.rules"] -> exophial's commit gate via exo-125). A checker no consumer's gate runs enforces nothing — "done = integrated", and the dispatching coordinator's pebble bodies under-specified integration; this pebble closes that gap.

THE WORK: port the four checkers to LibCST LintRule classes in the rule-pack, one rule per concern, mirroring the existing corpus:
1. FsmEnumDispatchExhaustive (from scripts/check_asp_fsm_enum_dispatch.py) — reject; placement per docs/design.md taxonomy.
2. FsmEdgeDuration (from scripts/check_edge_duration.py) — reject.
3. FsmRedundantBranches (from scripts/check_asp_fsm_redundant_branches.py) — warn-severity semantics (the corpus convention for advisory rules).
4. FsmStringlyDispatch (from scripts/check_stringly_dispatch.py) — warn; keep the "# asp-fsm: boundary-parse" opt-out.

Placement note: rules/__init__.py documents fixit's flat-only discovery — a new module or catalog/ one-rule-per-file entries must be re-exported at the aspergillus.rules level exactly as the ASP4xx catalog rules are. Reuse the existing VALID/INVALID fixture idiom (add_lint_rule_tests_to_module in python/tests) — the merged tests/fixtures/*.py files become rule fixtures. Assign ASP4xx (or per-design) rule numbers and update README.md + docs/design.md rule tables.

RETIRE THE SCRIPTS: delete scripts/check_asp_fsm_enum_dispatch.py, check_asp_fsm_redundant_branches.py, check_edge_duration.py, check_stringly_dispatch.py once the LintRules carry the behavior (one code path, not two; grep for any references before deleting).

ACCEPTANCE (the integrated end state, not artifact existence):
(a) uv run --directory python fixit lint <fixture-with-if/elif-enum-dispatch> reports the exhaustive-dispatch violation through the REAL fixit CLI with the repo's own [tool.fixit] config — the same independent-verification bar asp-6b0 used for ASP410;
(b) the same CLI run flags an edge-duration fixture and warns on redundant/stringly fixtures;
(c) valid shapes (match+assert_never, boundary-marker opt-out, renamed-variable branches) produce NO report;
(d) full suite green: uv run --directory python pytest tests -q, including the new add_lint_rule_tests_to_module coverage;
(e) the four scripts/ checkers are gone and nothing references them;
(f) README.md + docs/design.md list the new rules in the taxonomy tables.
